    "markdown": "## Classification\n- **Type**: Institutional Space\n- **Layer**: Delirium Space\n\n## Description\nThe Hospital is a common deliriant setting—a maze-like medical facility where the operative wanders, confused, encountering false medical staff and patients.\n\n## Characteristics\n- **Layout**: Maze-like, confusing, endless corridors\n- **Lighting**: Harsh fluorescent, flickering\n- **Sound**: Beeps, footsteps, distant voices\n- **Smell**: Antiseptic, medical\n- **Atmosphere**: Anxiety, confusion, vulnerability\n\n## Areas\n- **The Corridors**: Endless, identical, confusing\n- **The Rooms**: Hospital rooms, occupied or empty\n- **The Nurses' Station**: Staff, watching, judging\n- **The Waiting Room**: Endless waiting\n- **The Operating Room**: Threat, vulnerability\n\n## Associated Entities\n- False nurses, doctors, patients, Shadow People\n\n## Function\n- **Primary**: Delirium manifestation\n- **Secondary**: Vulnerability, medical anxiety\n- **Tertiary**: Test of reality discrimination\n\n## Coping Strategies\n- **Reality testing**: Remind self it's hallucination\n- **Sitter**: Have someone reassure\n- **Grounding**: Return to body, breath\n- **Change setting**: Move to different room\n\n## Cosmological Position\n- **Layer**: Delirium Space\n- **Function**: Medical anxiety manifestation\n- **Parallel**: Hospital phobia, medical trauma",
