    "summary": "True hallucinations are perceptions that are indistinguishable from reality—unlike the geometric patterns of psychedelics, these appear as solid, real objects, people, or creatures.",
    "markdown": "## Classification\n- **Type**: Perceptual Phenomenon\n- **Phase**: Delirium State\n\n## Description\nTrue hallucinations are perceptions that are indistinguishable from reality—unlike the geometric patterns of psychedelics, these appear as solid, real objects, people, or creatures.\n\n## Characteristics\n- **Realism**: Indistinguishable from actual perception\n- **Solidity**: Appear three-dimensional, physical\n- **Persistence**: Don't fade when focused on\n- **Integration**: Fit into normal reality seamlessly\n- **Conviction**: Operative believes they are real\n\n## Types\n- **Visual**: Seeing people, animals, objects\n- **Auditory**: Hearing voices, sounds, music\n- **Tactile**: Feeling touches, crawling sensations\n- **Olfactory**: Smelling scents, odors\n- **Gustatory**: Tasting flavors\n\n## Common Manifestations\n- **Insects**: Spiders, ants, bugs\n- **People**: Known or unknown individuals\n- **Animals**: Pets, creatures\n- **Objects**: Items that don't exist\n- **Scenarios**: Complex situations, events\n\n## Distinguishing from Reality\n- **Inconsistencies**: Small details wrong\n- **Impossibility**: Violates physical laws\n- **Sitter input**: Others can't see them\n- **Reality testing**: Check physical evidence\n\n## Function\n- **Primary**: Delirium state indicator\n- **Secondary**: Reality testing challenge\n- **Tertiary**: Psychological material manifestation",
    "sourcePath": "wiki/Deliriants/Phenomena/True_Hallucinations.md",
    "safetyRedacted": false
