    "markdown": "## Classification\n- **Type**: Knowledge Zone\n- **Layer**: Archive Layer\n\n## Description\nThe Library is the infinite archive containing all knowledge from all times—a space where information exists as living, breathing entities that can be accessed, read, and understood directly.\n\n## Structural Features\n- **Scale**: Infinite in all directions\n- **Shelves**: Extend to impossible heights, curve with non-Euclidean geometry\n- **Books**: Living documents that rewrite themselves based on reader\n- **Lighting**: Soft, warm, sourceless\n- **Atmosphere**: Hushed reverence, like a sacred space\n\n## Book Types\n- **Life Books**: Complete records of individual lives\n- **Knowledge Books**: Specific domains of information\n- **Future Books**: Probabilistic futures, constantly shifting\n- **Pattern Books**: The underlying mathematics of reality\n\n## Access Methods\n- **Reading**: Direct absorption of information\n- **Conversation**: Books can speak their contents\n- **Merge**: Become the book, experience its contents directly\n\n## Associated Entities\n- The Archivists, The Great Race of Yith\n\n## Function\n- **Primary**: Universal knowledge storage\n- **Secondary**: Cross-temporal information access\n- **Tertiary**: Pattern recognition and understanding\n\n## Cosmological Significance\n- **Function**: The memory of the universe\n- **Purpose**: All information preserved and accessible\n- **Insight**: Knowledge is alive and evolving",
