    "summary": "The Hum is the fundamental carrier wave of the DMT experience—a low-frequency vibration that underlies all other phenomena and serves as the \"soundtrack\" to the journey.",
    "markdown": "## Classification\n- **Type**: Auditory Phenomenon\n- **Phase**: All phases\n\n## Description\nThe Hum is the fundamental carrier wave of the DMT experience—a low-frequency vibration that underlies all other phenomena and serves as the \"soundtrack\" to the journey.\n\n## Characteristics\n- **Frequency**: 40-80 Hz range (theta-delta border)\n- **Quality**: Deep, resonant, organic\n- **Source**: Seems to come from everywhere and nowhere\n- **Intensity**: Builds from subtle to overwhelming\n\n## Variations\n- **The Didgeridoo**: Deep, breathy, pulsing\n- **The Bell**: Clear, ringing, crystalline\n- **The Choir**: Multiple voices in harmony\n- **The Machine**: Mechanical, rhythmic, industrial\n\n## Function\n- **Primary**: Carrier wave for information\n- **Secondary**: Entrainment of brainwaves\n- **Tertiary**: Navigation beacon\n\n## Associated Phenomena\n- **Physical vibration**: Body resonates with frequency\n- **Visual sync**: Patterns pulse in time with hum\n- **Emotional modulation**: Frequency affects emotional state\n\n## Technical Notes\n- **Brainwave correlation**: Theta-delta range associated with deep meditation\n- **Binaural potential**: May be related to binaural beat effects\n- **Universal report**: Nearly all operatives report some form of hum",
