    "markdown": "## Classification\n- **Type**: Temporal Phenomenon\n- **Phase**: All phases\n\n## Description\nTime dilation is the dramatic distortion of temporal perception during DMT experiences—subjective time expanding to fill what objectively is only minutes.\n\n## Types\n- **Expansion**: Subjective time longer than objective (most common)\n- **Contraction**: Subjective time shorter than objective (rare)\n- **Non-linearity**: Past, present, future accessible simultaneously\n- **Eternity**: Sense of existing outside of time\n\n## Ratios\n- **Mild**: 2:1 (subjective:objective)\n- **Moderate**: 5:1 to 10:1\n- **Extreme**: 100:1 to infinite\n- **Eternal**: No time at all—pure present\n\n## Associated Phenomena\n- **The Eternal Moment**: Single moment stretched to infinity\n- **Life Review**: Entire life experienced in an instant\n- **Future Preview**: Probabilistic futures accessible\n- **Past Access**: Historical events as present experience\n\n## Function\n- **Primary**: Allows deep processing in short objective time\n- **Secondary**: Access to normally inaccessible time scales\n- **Tertiary**: Teaching about the nature of time\n\n## Technical Notes\n- **Neural basis**: May involve disruption of time-keeping brain regions\n- **Quantum possibility**: May reflect actual temporal flexibility\n- **Evolutionary**: Allows rapid learning and adaptation",
