    "summary": "Reality consists of multiple dimensions beyond the familiar 3D space + time. DMT allows access to these higher dimensions.",
    "markdown": "## Classification\n- **Type**: Technical Framework\n- **Domain**: Spatial Geometry\n\n## Core Concept\nReality consists of multiple dimensions beyond the familiar 3D space + time. DMT allows access to these higher dimensions.\n\n## Dimension Model\n- **3D**: Our normal spatial experience\n- **4D**: Space + time (Einsteinian spacetime)\n- **5D+:**: Higher spatial dimensions, accessible during DMT\n\n## Accessed Dimensions\n- **4D**: Time as navigable dimension\n- **5D**: Probability space—all possible timelines\n- **6D**: Phase space—configuration of all possible states\n- **7D+:**: Unknown, ineffable dimensions\n\n## Characteristics of Higher Dimensions\n- **Non-Euclidean geometry**: Parallel lines meet, angles don't sum to 180°\n- **Impossible objects**: Structures that can't exist in 3D\n- **Overlapping spaces**: Multiple locations simultaneously\n- **Infinite recursion**: Fractal structure at all scales\n\n## Navigation\n- **Intention**: Thought directs movement\n- **Emotion**: Emotional state affects location\n- **Surrender**: Letting go allows deeper access\n- **Fear**: Blocks access, creates barriers\n\n## Entity Correlation\n- **3D entities**: Physical beings\n- **4D entities**: Time travelers, prophets\n- **5D+ entities**: Higher-dimensional beings (most DMT entities)\n\n## Technical Notes\n- **Mathematical basis**: String theory, M-theory propose 10-11 dimensions\n- **Brain correlation**: May involve access to normally unused neural pathways\n- **Evolutionary**: Potential future human capacity",
    "sourcePath": "wiki/DMT/Technical/Dimensional_Architecture.md",
    "safetyRedacted": false
