    "markdown": "## Classification\n- **Type**: Cosmological Model\n- **Domain**: Metaphysical Framework\n\n## Core Tenet\nReality as we experience it is a simulation running on a computational substrate that exists \"outside\" our perceived universe. DMT provides access to this underlying architecture.\n\n## Key Concepts\n- **The Matrix**: The simulated reality we inhabit\n- **The Source**: The computational substrate running the simulation\n- **The Code**: The underlying programming of reality\n- **The Glitch**: Errors or anomalies in the simulation\n- **The Hack**: Ways to access or modify the code\n\n## DMT Evidence\n- **Geometric visuals**: Evidence of underlying grid/pixel structure\n- **Entity encounters**: NPCs or other conscious agents in the simulation\n- **Downloads**: Direct access to source code/information\n- **Reality manipulation**: Temporary modification of simulation parameters\n- **Time dilation**: Variable processing speed of the simulation\n\n## Implications\n- **Free will**: May be limited by programming\n- **Afterlife**: Could be transfer to different simulation or level\n- **Purpose**: Simulation may have specific goals or parameters\n- **Creators**: Unknown entities running the simulation\n\n## Technical Specs\n- **Resolution**: Planck length as pixel size\n- **Frame rate**: Planck time as refresh rate\n- **Processing**: Quantum computation\n- **Memory**: Holographic storage\n\n## Cosmological Position\n- **Function**: Explanatory framework for DMT phenomena\n- **Purpose**: Understanding the nature of reality\n- **Limitations**: May be metaphor rather than literal truth",
    "sourcePath": "wiki/DMT/Technical/The_Simulation_Hypothesis.md",
    "safetyRedacted": false
