    "markdown": "## Classification\n- **Type**: Dose-Dependent States\n- **Domain**: DXM Experience Structure\n\n## Description\nThe Plateaus are the distinct levels of DXM experience, each with characteristic effects, intensity, and qualitative differences.\n\n## First Plateau (1.5-2.5 mg/kg)\n- **Mood lift**: Euphoria, stimulation\n- **Music enhancement**: Enhanced appreciation\n- **Mild dissociation**: Slight distance\n- **Social**: Can still interact\n- **Duration**: 2-4 hours\n\n## Second Plateau (2.5-7.5 mg/kg)\n- **Strong dissociation**: Clear separation\n- **Cognitive changes**: Altered thinking\n- **Closed-eye visuals**: Patterned visuals\n- **Robo-walk**: Uncoordinated movement\n- **Duration**: 3-6 hours\n\n## Third Plateau (7.5-15 mg/kg)\n- **Deep dissociation**: Out-of-body possible\n- **Profound visuals**: Complex scenes\n- **Ego effects**: Significant ego dissolution\n- **Flange**: Prominent auditory distortion\n- **Duration**: 6-8 hours\n\n## Fourth Plateau (15+ mg/kg)\n- **Complete dissociation**: Out-of-body common\n- **Ego death**: Complete dissolution\n- **Mystical experiences**: Transcendent states\n- **Danger zone**: Higher risk\n- **Duration**: 8-12+ hours\n\n## Sigma Plateau (Redosing)\n- **Not a true plateau**: From repeated dosing\n- **Unique effects**: Different from single dose\n- **Psychotomimetic**: Can mimic psychosis\n- **Not recommended**: Unpredictable, risky\n\n## Plateau Navigation\n- **Start low**: Learn your response\n- **Respect each level**: Don't rush\n- **Set and setting**: More important at higher levels\n- **Sitter**: Essential for 3rd and 4th",
    "sourcePath": "wiki/DXM/Phenomena/The_Plateaus.md",
